                <pb facs="1000" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/208:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-12T17:00:00-05:45">June 12, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Department’s June 11, 5 p.m., and last paragraph of my 91, May 29, 3 p.m.
                    May I advise this Government at the same time that Captain Johnson will resign
                    the position of President of the National Board of Elections and thus enable
                    this Government to complete the organization of the board? I suggest that the
                    reply be submitted by cable as this Government is anxious to have the board
                    resume its duties as early as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
